e results list, count, sort, load-more, and error/empty-state messaging. Pre-populated with a sensible default; rearrange, remove, or add more from the inserter. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Container for the search results region — bundles the results list, count, sort, load-more, and error/empty-state messaging. Pre-populated with a sensible default; rearrange, remove, or add more from the inserter. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block descriptionText input for the search query. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Text input for the search query. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block descriptionControls the order of search results. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Controls the order of search results. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleSort By'=>'Sort By','block descriptionLoads the next page of results. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Loads the next page of results. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleResults List'=>'Results List','block descriptionDisplays the results count. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Displays the results count. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block keywordcolophon'=>'colophon','block keywordpowered by'=>'powered by','block keywordjetpack'=>'jetpack','block descriptionRenders the "Search powered by Jetpack" attribution link to jetpack.com. Free-plan sites always display this; paid sites can remove the block to hide it.'=>'Renders the "Search powered by Jetpack" attribution link to jetpack.com. Free-plan sites always display this; paid sites can remove the block to hide it.','block titlePowered by Jetpack'=>'Powered by Jetpack','block descriptionVertical stack of filter blocks. Pre-populated with the most common filters; rearrange, remove, or add more from the inserter. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Vertical stack of filter blocks. Pre-populated with the most common filters; rearrange, remove, or add more from the inserter. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block keywordsidebar'=>'sidebar','block keywordproduct'=>'product','block keywordwoocommerce'=>'woocommerce','block descriptionA composable container for WooCommerce-style product filters (status, rating, price, attributes). Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'A composable container for WooCommerce-style product filters (status, rating, price, attributes). Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleProduct Filters'=>'Product Filters','block descriptionTucks the filters behind a compact button that opens them in a popover. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Tucks the filters behind a compact button that opens them in a popover. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleCollapsible Filters'=>'Collapsible Filters','block descriptionLet shoppers narrow product results to in-stock items. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Let shoppers narrow product results to in-stock items. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleFilter by Stock Status'=>'Filter by Stock Status','block descriptionLet shoppers filter products by star rating. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Let shoppers filter products by star rating. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleFilter by Rating'=>'Filter by Rating','block variation descriptionDraggable range slider paired with min/max number inputs. Mirrors WooCommerce Blocks’ price slider.'=>'Draggable range slider paired with min/max number inputs. Mirrors WooCommerce Blocks’ price slider.','block variation titleFilter by Price (Slider)'=>'Filter by Price (Slider)','block variation descriptionTwo number inputs, joined by an em-dash. Compact — best when a slider would take too much vertical space.'=>'Two number inputs, joined by an em-dash. Compact — best when a slider would take too much vertical space.','block variation titleFilter by Price'=>'Filter by Price','block descriptionLet shoppers filter products by price. Either two number inputs or a draggable range slider with paired inputs. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Let shoppers filter products by price. Either two number inputs or a draggable range slider with paired inputs. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleFilter by Price'=>'Filter by Price','block descriptionLet shoppers filter products by a WooCommerce attribute (color, size, …). Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Let shoppers filter products by a WooCommerce attribute (colour, size, …). Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleFilter by Product Attribute'=>'Filter by Product Attribute','block descriptionDate filter. Group results into yearly or monthly buckets so visitors can scope a search to a single time window. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Date filter. Group results into yearly or monthly buckets so visitors can scope a search to a single time window. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleFilter by Date'=>'Filter by Date','block descriptionCheckbox filter. Use a variation (Category, Tag, Post Type, Author, Product Category, Product Tag, Product Brand, Custom Taxonomy) or configure manually. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Checkbox filter. Use a variation (Category, Tag, Post Type, Author, Product Category, Product Tag, Product Brand, Custom Taxonomy) or configure manually. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block style labelDefault'=>'Default','block descriptionA button that clears every active filter. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'A button that clears every active filter. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleClear Filters'=>'Clear Filters','block descriptionShow an AI-generated answer above the search results, with citations and an optional Show more / extended answer flow. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Show an AI-generated answer above the search results, with citations and an optional Show more / extended answer flow. Powered by Jetpack Search.','block titleAI Answer'=>'AI Answer','block descriptionPills showing the currently selected filters. Powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'Pills showing the currently selected filters. Powered by Jetpack Search.','Set'=>'Set','Not set'=>'Not set','← Previous'=>'← Previous','Activity Log'=>'Activity Log','WP.com call failed.'=>'WP.com call failed.','Could not remove the comp.'=>'Could not remove the comp.','Could not comp the subscription.'=>'Could not comp the subscription.','Could not add subscribers.'=>'Could not add subscribers.','Provide at least one valid email address.'=>'Provide at least one valid email address.','Provide either a subscription_id or a user_id.'=>'Provide either a subscription_id or a user_id.','No subscriber identifiers were provided.'=>'No subscriber identifiers were provided.','Could not fetch subscriber totals.'=>'Could not fetch subscriber totals.','Could not fetch subscribers.'=>'Could not fetch subscribers.','You are not allowed to view subscribers for this site.'=>'You are not allowed to view subscribers for this site.','The current user is not connected to Jetpack. Connect the user to Jetpack before configuring Monitor notifications.'=>'The current user is not connected to Jetpack. Connect the user to Jetpack before configuring Monitor notifications.','The Monitor module is not active. Activate it before configuring notifications.'=>'The Monitor module is not active. Activate it before configuring notifications.','The enabled parameter must be a boolean. Strings like "true" / "false" are not accepted.'=>'The enabled parameter must be a boolean. Strings like "true" / "false" are not accepted.','A desired enabled state (boolean) is required.'=>'A desired enabled state (boolean) is required.','The remote Jetpack Monitor service is unreachable. Retry shortly; this is typically transient.'=>'The remote Jetpack Monitor service is unreachable. Retry shortly; this is typically transient.','User is not connected to Jetpack. Connect first via the My Jetpack admin page, then retry this ability.'=>'User is not connected to Jetpack. Connect first via the My Jetpack admin page, then retry this ability.','The Monitor module is not active. Activate it before reading Monitor status.'=>'The Monitor module is not active. Activate it before reading Monitor status.','Desired notification state. true enables downtime email notifications for the current user; false disables them.'=>'Desired notification state. true enables downtime email notifications for the current user; false disables them.','Enable or disable downtime email notifications for the current user. Idempotent — setting the state to the current value returns changed=false. Returns { enabled, changed }. Preconditions: the Monitor module must be active and the current user must be connected to Jetpack; call jetpack-monitor/get-monitor-status first to verify the connection. Fails with jetpack_monitor_module_inactive (activate the Monitor module first — these abilities are only registered while the module is active, so this error indicates a race) or jetpack_monitor_not_connected when preconditions are not met.'=>'Enable or disable downtime email notifications for the current user. Idempotent — setting the state to the current value returns changed=false. Returns { enabled, changed }. Preconditions: the Monitor module must be active and the current user must be connected to Jetpack; call jetpack-monitor/get-monitor-status first to verify the connection. Fails with jetpack_monitor_module_inactive (activate the Monitor module first — these abilities are only registered while the module is active, so this error indicates a race) or jetpack_monitor_not_connected when preconditions are not met.','Set Jetpack Monitor notifications'=>'Set Jetpack Monitor notifications','Return the current Downtime Monitor state as { module_active, user_connected, notifications_enabled, last_status_change }. notifications_enabled is a boolean (does the current user receive downtime alerts). last_status_change is the timestamp of the most recent up/down status transition recorded by the Monitor service, as a "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss" UTC string, or null when no transition has been recorded — this reflects the legacy last_status_change projection, not necessarily the last time downtime began. Fails with jetpack_monitor_not_connected when the current user is not connected to Jetpack (connect first via the My Jetpack admin page), or jetpack_monitor_service_unreachable when the remote Monitor service cannot be reached. These abilities are only registered while the Monitor module is active; if they are absent from wp_get_abilities(), activate the Monitor module first.'=>'Return the current Downtime Monitor state as { module_active, user_connected, notifications_enabled, last_status_change }. notifications_enabled is a boolean (does the current user receive downtime alerts). last_status_change is the timestamp of the most recent up/down status transition recorded by the Monitor service, as a "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss" UTC string, or null when no transition has been recorded — this reflects the legacy last_status_change projection, not necessarily the last time downtime began. Fails with jetpack_monitor_not_connected when the current user is not connected to Jetpack (connect first via the My Jetpack admin page), or jetpack_monitor_service_unreachable when the remote Monitor service cannot be reached. These abilities are only registered while the Monitor module is active; if they are absent from wp_get_abilities(), activate the Monitor module first.','Get Jetpack Monitor status'=>'Get Jetpack Monitor status','Dispatch a full sitemap regeneration by scheduling the existing `jp_sitemap_cron_hook` cron event. Returns { dispatched, status, next_scheduled_at } where status is one of "queued" (a single-event cron tick was just scheduled), "running" (a build is already in flight per the `jetpack-sitemap-state-lock` transient), or "already_running" (alias of "running"; surfaced so callers can branch on either spelling). `next_scheduled_at` is the next `jp_sitemap_cron_hook` tick as an ISO 8601 UTC string with an explicit `Z` zone designator (e.g. `2026-05-19T19:33:20Z`), or null when nothing is scheduled (e.g. status=running with no future tick queued) — it tells the caller when the build they queued (or the one already pending) will actually run. Idempotent — calling this while a build is already in flight or already queued returns dispatched=false and the matching status rather than stacking duplicate cron events.'=>'Dispatch a full sitemap regeneration by scheduling the existing `jp_sitemap_cron_hook` cron event. Returns { dispatched, status, next_scheduled_at } where status is one of "queued" (a single-event cron tick was just scheduled), "running" (a build is already in flight per the `jetpack-sitemap-state-lock` transient), or "already_running" (alias of "running"; surfaced so callers can branch on either spelling). `next_scheduled_at` is the next `jp_sitemap_cron_hook` tick as an ISO 8601 UTC string with an explicit `Z` zone designator (e.g. `2026-05-19T19:33:20Z`), or null when nothing is scheduled (e.g. status=running with no future tick queued) — it tells the caller when the build they queued (or the one already pending) will actually run. Idempotent — calling this while a build is already in flight or already queued returns dispatched=false and the matching status rather than stacking duplicate cron events.','Request a Jetpack Sitemaps rebuild'=>'Request a Jetpack Sitemaps rebuild','Return the current state of the Jetpack-generated XML sitemaps as { active, url, post_count, page_count, news_sitemap_enabled, sitemaps }. `active` reflects whether the Sitemaps module is on. `url` is the public sitemap.xml entry point. `post_count` / `page_count` are the published `post` / `page` counts (the same baseline the WordPress core sitemap uses). `news_sitemap_enabled` reflects the `jetpack_news_sitemap_include_in_robotstxt` filter (default true). `sitemaps` is the list of child sitemaps actually present in the served sitemap.xml index — each entry is `{ loc, lastmod }`, where `lastmod` is the W3C datetime string the sitemap exposes (or null when that entry omits one). `sitemaps` is an empty array until a master sitemap has been generated. These abilities are only registered while the Sitemaps module is active; if they are absent from wp_get_abilities(), activate the Sitemaps module first.'=>'Return the current state of the Jetpack-generated XML sitemaps as { active, url, post_count, page_count, news_sitemap_enabled, sitemaps }. `active` reflects whether the Sitemaps module is on. `url` is the public sitemap.xml entry point. `post_count` / `page_count` are the published `post` / `page` counts (the same baseline the WordPress core sitemap uses). `news_sitemap_enabled` reflects the `jetpack_news_sitemap_include_in_robotstxt` filter (default true). `sitemaps` is the list of child sitemaps actually present in the served sitemap.xml index — each entry is `{ loc, lastmod }`, where `lastmod` is the W3C datetime string the sitemap exposes (or null when that entry omits one). `sitemaps` is an empty array until a master sitemap has been generated. These abilities are only registered while the Sitemaps module is active; if they are absent from wp_get_abilities(), activate the Sitemaps module first.','Get Jetpack Sitemaps status'=>'Get Jetpack Sitemaps status','No Jetpack/WordPress.com blog ID is available for this site. Connect Jetpack before requesting wp.me shortlinks.'=>'No Jetpack/WordPress.com blog ID is available for this site. Connect Jetpack before requesting wp.me shortlinks.','When true, prepend a single entry for the site homepage (post_id 0, post_type "blog") to the response.'=>'When true, prepend a single entry for the site homepage (post_id 0, post_type "blog") to the response.','Up to 100 post IDs to fetch shortlinks for. Order is preserved in the response. Defaults to an empty list.'=>'Up to 100 post IDs to fetch shortlinks for. Order is preserved in the response. Defaults to an empty list.','Return wp.me shortlinks for the given posts and (optionally) the site homepage. Each result is a { post_id, post_title, post_type, shortlink, target_url } object — post_id is 0 for the homepage entry, post_type is "blog". IDs that do not exist, are unreadable to the current user, or belong to a post type without shortlinks support are silently omitted (returns a shorter array, not WP_Error). Caps post_ids at 100 per call. Requires the WP.me Shortlinks Jetpack module (slug: shortlinks) to be active and the site to be connected; an unconnected site returns jetpack_shortlinks_blog_id_unavailable. Use jetpack/get-modules to verify the module is on, jetpack/set-module-status to activate it.'=>'Return wp.me shortlinks for the given posts and (optionally) the site homepage. Each result is a { post_id, post_title, post_type, shortlink, target_url } object — post_id is 0 for the homepage entry, post_type is "blog". IDs that do not exist, are unreadable to the current user, or belong to a post type without shortlinks support are silently omitted (returns a shorter array, not WP_Error). Caps post_ids at 100 per call. Requires the WP.me Shortlinks Jetpack module (slug: shortlinks) to be active and the site to be connected; an unconnected site returns jetpack_shortlinks_blog_id_unavailable. Use jetpack/get-modules to verify the module is on, jetpack/set-module-status to activate it.','Get wp.me shortlinks'=>'Get wp.me shortlinks','The canonical permalink the shortlink resolves to.'=>'The canonical permalink the shortlink resolves to.','The wp.me URL.'=>'The wp.me URL.','"blog" for the homepage entry; otherwise the WordPress post type slug (post, page, attachment, or a CPT that supports shortlinks).'=>'"blog" for the homepage entry; otherwise the WordPress post type slug (post, page, attachment, or a CPT that supports shortlinks).','0 for the site homepage entry; otherwise the WordPress post ID.'=>'0 for the site homepage entry; otherwise the WordPress post ID.','Abilities for retrieving wp.me shortlinks for posts, pages, attachments, and the site homepage.'=>'Abilities for retrieving wp.me shortlinks for posts, pages, attachments, and the site homepage.','You are not allowed to fetch related posts for this post.'=>'You are not allowed to fetch related posts for this post.','Unknown post ID. Verify the post exists and is accessible.'=>'Unknown post ID. Verify the post exists and is accessible.','A post_id is required to fetch related posts.'=>'A post_id is required to fetch related posts.','Post IDs to exclude from the result.'=>'Post IDs to exclude from the result.','Restrict matches to a single post type slug (e.g. "post", "page"). Defaults to the source post\'s type.'=>'Restrict matches to a single post type slug (e.g. "post", "page"). Defaults to the source post\'s type.','Deprecated alias for per_page. Defaults to 3 when per_page is omitted. Capped at 20.'=>'Deprecated alias for per_page. Defaults to 3 when per_page is omitted. Capped at 20.','Maximum number of related posts to return per call. Must be between 1 and 20 — the Elasticsearch backend hard-caps results at 20, so larger values are not supported and pagination past the first 20 results is unavailable. Defaults to 20.'=>'Maximum number of related posts to return per call. Must be between 1 and 20 — the Elasticsearch back end hard-caps results at 20, so larger values are not supported and pagination past the first 20 results is unavailable. Defaults to 20.','WordPress post ID to find related posts for. Must reference an existing post.'=>'WordPress post ID to find related posts for. Must reference an existing post.','Return related posts for a single post as an array of { id, url, title, excerpt, date, post_type, format }. The caller must be able to edit the source post (edit_post capability); unauthorized requests return jetpack_related_posts_forbidden. Backed by Elasticsearch via the Jetpack connection: when Related Posts is disabled, the post is unknown, or the ES backend is unreachable, the array is empty (not an error). Use per_page to control the result count (1..20, default 20); the underlying Elasticsearch query is hard-capped at 20, so values above 20 are rejected by the input schema and pagination beyond the first 20 results is not supported. The legacy "size" alias is accepted for backward compatibility and defaults to 3 when no per_page is supplied. Read-only and idempotent. Use jetpack/get-modules to confirm the related-posts module is active, jetpack/set-module-status to activate it.'=>'Return related posts for a single post as an array of { id, url, title, excerpt, date, post_type, format }. The caller must be able to edit the source post (edit_post capability); unauthorised requests return jetpack_related_posts_forbidden. Backed by Elasticsearch via the Jetpack connection: when Related Posts is disabled, the post is unknown, or the ES backend is unreachable, the array is empty (not an error). Use per_page to control the result count (1..20, default 20); the underlying Elasticsearch query is hard-capped at 20, so values above 20 are rejected by the input schema and pagination beyond the first 20 results is not supported. The legacy "size" alias is accepted for backward compatibility and defaults to 3 when no per_page is supplied. Read-only and idempotent. Use jetpack/get-modules to confirm the related-posts module is active, jetpack/set-module-status to activate it.','Get related posts'=>'Get related posts','Abilities for reading related posts.'=>'Abilities for reading related posts.','Unable to fetch VideoPress stats.'=>'Unable to fetch VideoPress stats.','Starting date for range queries (YYYY-MM-DD).'=>'Starting date for range queries (YYYY-MM-DD).','Most recent day to include in results (YYYY-MM-DD).'=>'Most recent day to include in results (YYYY-MM-DD).','Number of periods to include.'=>'Number of periods to include.','Period unit: day, week, month, or year.'=>'Period unit: day, week, month, or year.','Invalid Activity Log event payload.'=>'Invalid Activity Log event payload.','You do not have the correct user permissions to access Activity Log events.'=>'You do not have the correct user permissions to access Activity Log events.','Activity Log Event'=>'Activity 