ue.','Unable to fetch Scan data.'=>'Unable to fetch Scan data.','Site is not connected to WordPress.com.'=>'Site is not connected to WordPress.com.','You do not have permission to access this resource.'=>'You do not have permission to access this resource.','Connection identifier echoed back from the request.'=>'Connection identifier echoed back from the request.','Edited post content.'=>'Edited post content.','Edited post excerpt.'=>'Edited post excerpt.','Edited post title.'=>'Edited post title.','Edited post fields to use when rendering unsaved preview changes.'=>'Edited post fields to use when rendering unsaved preview changes.','Optional message override. Empty walks the per-connection / site / network-default chain.'=>'Optional message override. Empty walks the per-connection / site / network-default chain.','Publicize connection ID — used to dispatch the renderer and resolve the per-connection template.'=>'Publicise connection ID — used to dispatch the renderer and resolve the per-connection template.','Human-readable description of the placeholder.'=>'Human-readable description of the placeholder.','The placeholder token (e.g. {title}).'=>'The placeholder token (e.g. {title}).','Per-connection message templates require an upgraded plan.'=>'Per-connection message templates require an upgraded plan.','Per-connection message template override. Empty string means fall back to the global template.'=>'Per-connection message template override. Empty string means fall back to the global template.','Orders cannot be deleted via the REST API.'=>'Orders cannot be deleted via the REST API.','Orders cannot be modified via the REST API.'=>'Orders cannot be modified via the REST API.','Orders can only be created through the payment processing flow.'=>'Orders can only be created through the payment processing flow.','Your Daily Writing Prompt widget requires JavaScript to function properly.'=>'Your Daily Writing Prompt widget requires JavaScript to function properly.','Daily Writing Prompt'=>'Daily Writing Prompt','The site token used to authenticate with WordPress.com could not be validated.'=>'The site token used to authenticate with WordPress.com could not be validated.','We recommend either upgrading the user (%s) or reconnecting your site to WordPress.com.'=>'We recommend either upgrading the user (%s) or reconnecting your site to WordPress.com.','The site is connected to WordPress.com without a user. No connection owner to check.'=>'The site is connected to WordPress.com without a user. No connection owner to check.','Your site is not connected to WordPress.com. No connection owner to check.'=>'Your site is not connected to WordPress.com. No connection owner to check.','Your site is in Offline Mode.'=>'Your site is in Offline Mode.','The site token used to authenticate with WordPress.com is missing.'=>'The site token used to authenticate with WordPress.com is missing.','Your site is not connected to WordPress.com. No site token to check.'=>'Your site is not connected to WordPress.com. No site token to check.','Jetpack Connection'=>'Jetpack Connection','The Jetpack Connection\'s async local testing suite passed all tests!'=>'The Jetpack Connection\'s async local testing suite passed all tests!','Jetpack Connection passed all async tests.'=>'Jetpack Connection passed all async tests.','Your site is in Offline Mode:'=>'Your site is in Offline Mode:','The site is not in Offline Mode.'=>'The site is not in Offline Mode.','We recommend reconnecting your site to WordPress.com.'=>'We recommend reconnecting your site to WordPress.com.','A healthy Jetpack Connection allows connected plugins (such as Jetpack and WooCommerce) to provide features like Stats, Site Security, and Payments to your site.'=>'A healthy Jetpack Connection allows connected plugins (such as Jetpack and WooCommerce) to provide features like Stats, Site Security, and Payments to your site.','Reconnect now'=>'Reconnect now','Connecting a WordPress.com account unlocks features for Jetpack and Automattic for Agencies including secure logins.'=>'Connecting a WordPress.com account unlocks features for Jetpack and Automattic for Agencies including secure logins.','Connecting a WordPress.com account unlocks features for Jetpack and WooCommerce including secure logins.'=>'Connecting a WordPress.com account unlocks features for Jetpack and WooCommerce including secure logins.','Connecting a WordPress.com account unlocks features for Jetpack, WooCommerce, and Automattic for Agencies including secure logins.'=>'Connecting a WordPress.com account unlocks features for Jetpack, WooCommerce, and Automattic for Agencies including secure logins.','Jetpack Connection Tests'=>'Jetpack Connection Tests','Return the site-level Jetpack connection state in one zero-argument call. Shape: { site_registered, user_connected, master_user, blog_id, registration_url, connection_version }. `site_registered` is true when the site has a blog id and a blog token. `user_connected` is true when at least one user has linked their WordPress.com account. `master_user` is the local user id of the connection owner (the user who registered the site), or null if there is no owner. `blog_id` is the WordPress.com site id, or null when the site has not been registered. `registration_url` is the wp-admin URL the site owner should visit to register the site when `site_registered` is false; null once the site is registered. `connection_version` is the running Jetpack Connection package version. Read-only and idempotent — safe to poll.'=>'Return the site-level Jetpack connection state in one zero-argument call. Shape: { site_registered, user_connected, master_user, blog_id, registration_url, connection_version }. `site_registered` is true when the site has a blog id and a blog token. `user_connected` is true when at least one user has linked their WordPress.com account. `master_user` is the local user id of the connection owner (the user who registered the site), or null if there is no owner. `blog_id` is the WordPress.com site id, or null when the site has not been registered. `registration_url` is the wp-admin URL the site owner should visit to register the site when `site_registered` is false; null once the site is registered. `connection_version` is the running Jetpack Connection package version. Read-only and idempotent — safe to poll.','Get Jetpack connection status'=>'Get Jetpack connection status','Abilities provided by Jetpack.'=>'Abilities provided by Jetpack.','Backup enqueued. Use jetpack-backup/list-backups to monitor progress.'=>'Backup enqueued. Use jetpack-backup/list-backups to monitor progress.','The backup service did not accept the request. The connection to WordPress.com may be temporarily unavailable; retry shortly.'=>'The backup service did not accept the request. The connection to WordPress.com may be temporarily unavailable; retry shortly.','The `%s` parameter must be a valid ISO 8601 datetime (e.g. "2026-05-13T14:30:00Z").'=>'The `%s` parameter must be a valid ISO 8601 datetime (e.g. "2026-05-13T14:30:00Z").','Enqueue an on-demand backup of this site. Returns { enqueued: bool, message: string }. Each successful call queues a new backup job; this is a state-changing write, not idempotent. Use get-backup-overview or list-backups afterwards to track progress. Requires the manage_options capability. Returns jetpack_backup_data_unavailable when the upstream service rejects the request.'=>'Enqueue an on-demand backup of this site. Returns { enqueued: bool, message: string }. Each successful call queues a new backup job; this is a state-changing write, not idempotent. Use get-backup-overview or list-backups afterwards to track progress. Requires the manage_options capability. Returns jetpack_backup_data_unavailable when the upstream service rejects the request.','Request a backup'=>'Request a backup','Items per page (default 20, max 100).'=>'Items per page (default 20, max 100).','Page number, 1-based.'=>'Page number, 1-based.','Return only the restore with this id. Unknown ids yield an empty array.'=>'Return only the restore with this id. Unknown ids yield an empty array.','Return zero or more recent restore operations as an array. Each item: { id, rewind_id, started, last_updated, status, progress }. Pass id to fetch a single restore (returns 0- or 1-element array). Otherwise paginate with page and per_page (default 20, max 100). Read-only and idempotent.'=>'Return zero or more recent restore operations as an array. Each item: { id, rewind_id, started, last_updated, status, progress }. Pass id to fetch a single restore (returns 0- or 1-element array). Otherwise paginate with page and per_page (default 20, max 100). Read-only and idempotent.','List restores'=>'List restores','Cap on items returned per page (default 20, max 100). Also bounds the server-side query window the date filters are evaluated against.'=>'Cap on items returned per page (default 20, max 100). Also bounds the server-side query window the date filters are evaluated against.','1-based page number. Ignored when `id` or `date` is set (those are single-result lookups).'=>'1-based page number. Ignored when `id` or `date` is set (those are single-result lookups).','Filter by mapped status string (e.g. "finished", "error"). Applied client-side after the server query.'=>'Filter by mapped status string (e.g. "finished", "error"). Applied client-side after the server query.','How to interpret `date`. "on_or_before" (default; the latest backup at or before the target — typical for restores), "on_or_after" (earliest backup at or after), or "closest" (smallest absolute time difference). Ignored when `date` is not set.'=>'How to interpret `date`. "on_or_before" (default; the latest backup at or before the target — typical for restores), "on_or_after" (earliest backup at or after), or "closest" (smallest absolute time difference). Ignored when `date` is not set.','Target datetime to find a single matching backup. When set, the response is a 0- or 1-element array. Pair with `match` to choose direction.'=>'Target datetime to find a single matching backup. When set, the response is a 0- or 1-element array. Pair with `match` to choose direction.','Upper bound (inclusive) on backup `started` time. ISO 8601 datetime, e.g. "2026-04-30T23:59:59Z".'=>'Upper bound (inclusive) on backup `started` time. ISO 8601 datetime, e.g. "2026-04-30T23:59:59Z".','Lower bound (inclusive) on backup `started` time. ISO 8601 datetime, e.g. "2026-04-01T00:00:00Z".'=>'Lower bound (inclusive) on backup `started` time. ISO 8601 datetime, e.g. "2026-04-01T00:00:00Z".','Return only the backup with this rewind_id. Unknown ids yield an empty array.'=>'Return only the backup with this rewind_id. Unknown ids yield an empty array.','Return zero or more backups as an array. Each item summarises one backup: { id, rewind_id, started, last_updated, status, period, is_rewindable, has_warnings }. Combine filters to narrow the result without making multiple calls. `id` returns a 0- or 1-element array for a single rewind_id. `date_from` and `date_to` window the results (ISO 8601 datetimes; server-side filter). `date` + `match` ("on_or_before" default, "on_or_after", "closest") pick a single backup near a target datetime — useful for "find a restore point near this incident"; the response stays a 0- or 1-element array. `status` filters by mapped status (e.g. "finished", "error"). `page` + `per_page` paginate the result; iterate `page=1,2,...` until you get an empty array. A page may come back with fewer than `per_page` items even when more pages exist — `status` is applied client-side, and non-backup events are filtered out — so only an empty page reliably signals end of history. Read-only and idempotent. Backed by the wpcom activity-log feed.'=>'Return zero or more backups as an array. Each item summarises one backup: { id, rewind_id, started, last_updated, status, period, is_rewindable, has_warnings }. Combine filters to narrow the result without making multiple calls. `id` returns a 0- or 1-element array for a single rewind_id. `date_from` and `date_to` window the results (ISO 8601 datetimes; server-side filter). `date` + `match` ("on_or_before" default, "on_or_after", "closest") pick a single backup near a target datetime — useful for "find a restore point near this incident"; the response stays a 0- or 1-element array. `status` filters by mapped status (e.g. "finished", "error"). `page` + `per_page` paginate the result; iterate `page=1,2,...` until you get an empty array. A page may come back with fewer than `per_page` items even when more pages exist — `status` is applied client-side, and non-backup events are filtered out — so only an empty page reliably signals end of history. Read-only and idempotent. Backed by the wpcom activity-log feed.','List backups'=>'List backups','Return a single-call snapshot of the site backup state: { last_backup, recent_backup_count, schedule, storage }. Use this to answer "is my site protected?" before deciding whether to call list-backups, list-restores, or request-backup. Read-only and idempotent. Fields whose backing service is unreachable come back as null rather than failing the call. Requires the manage_options capability.'=>'Return a single-call snapshot of the site backup state: { last_backup, recent_backup_count, schedule, storage }. Use this to answer "is my site protected?" before deciding whether to call list-backups, list-restores, or request-backup. Read-only and idempotent. Fields whose backing service is unreachable come back as null rather than failing the call. Requires the manage_options capability.','Get backup overview'=>'Get backup overview','Site-wide management abilities (registered upstream).'=>'Site-wide management abilities (registered upstream).','Site'=>'Site','Cap on the number of events considered when collecting actors.'=>'Cap on the number of events considered when collecting actors.','Only return events performed by these 