etry after those preconditions are met.','Cannot activate the module while a conflicting plugin (%s) is active. Deactivate it on the WordPress Plugins screen, then retry.'=>'Cannot activate the module while a conflicting plugin (%s) is active. Deactivate it on the WordPress Plugins screen, then retry.','Unknown Jetpack module slug. Call jetpack/get-modules to enumerate valid slugs.'=>'Unknown Jetpack module slug. Call jetpack/get-modules to enumerate valid slugs.','The active parameter must be a boolean. Strings like "true" / "false" are not accepted.'=>'The active parameter must be a boolean. Strings like "true" / "false" are not accepted.','A desired active state (boolean) is required.'=>'A desired active state (boolean) is required.','A module slug is required. Call jetpack/get-modules to enumerate valid slugs.'=>'A module slug is required. Call jetpack/get-modules to enumerate valid slugs.','Desired active state. true activates the module; false deactivates it.'=>'Desired active state. true activates the module; false deactivates it.','The Jetpack module slug (e.g. "stats", "sso", "sharedaddy").'=>'The Jetpack module slug (e.g. "stats", "sso", "sharedaddy").','Set a Jetpack module\'s active state. Idempotent — setting a module to its current state returns changed=false. Returns { slug, active, changed }. Call jetpack/get-modules first to enumerate valid slugs. Modules requiring a Jetpack connection or a paid plan may fail with jetpack_modules_activate_failed; the message indicates the next step.'=>'Set a Jetpack module\'s active state. Idempotent — setting a module to its current state returns changed=false. Returns { slug, active, changed }. Call jetpack/get-modules first to enumerate valid slugs. Modules requiring a Jetpack connection or a paid plan may fail with jetpack_modules_activate_failed; the message indicates the next step.','Set Jetpack module status'=>'Set Jetpack module status','Case-insensitive substring match against the module name, slug, and description.'=>'Case-insensitive substring match against the module name, slug, and description.','Case-insensitive match against a module\'s feature tag (e.g. "Recommended", "Security", "Performance").'=>'Case-insensitive match against a module\'s feature tag (e.g. "Recommended", "Security", "Performance").','When set, only return modules whose current active state matches this value.'=>'When set, only return modules whose current active state matches this value.','Return a single module by slug. Unknown slugs yield an empty array.'=>'Return a single module by slug. Unknown slugs yield an empty array.','Return zero or more Jetpack modules as an array. Each element has { slug, name, description, active, sort, feature, plan_classes, requires_connection, requires_user_connection, auto_activate }. Combine slug / active / feature / search filters to narrow the list. When slug is provided and unknown, the result is an empty array (not an error). Use this before calling jetpack/set-module-status to enumerate legal slugs.'=>'Return zero or more Jetpack modules as an array. Each element has { slug, name, description, active, sort, feature, plan_classes, requires_connection, requires_user_connection, auto_activate }. Combine slug / active / feature / search filters to narrow the list. When slug is provided and unknown, the result is an empty array (not an error). Use this before calling jetpack/set-module-status to enumerate legal slugs.','Invalid value for "%1$s": %2$s'=>'Invalid value for "%1$s": %2$s','unsupported field type.'=>'unsupported field type.','must be %d characters or fewer.'=>'must be %d characters or fewer.','expected a string.'=>'expected a string.','allowed values are %s.'=>'allowed values are %s.','expected a boolean (true or false).'=>'expected a boolean (true or false).','WordPress.com did not return subscriber stats. Retry shortly.'=>'WordPress.com did not return subscriber stats. Retry shortly.','No Jetpack site ID is registered. Connect Jetpack and retry.'=>'No Jetpack site ID is registered. Connect Jetpack and retry.','Subscriber stats are only available on Jetpack-connected sites. Connect Jetpack and retry.'=>'Subscriber stats are only available on Jetpack-connected sites. Connect Jetpack and retry.','Return aggregate subscriber counts for the site. Always returns { all: int, email: int, paid: int }: all is the total subscriber count (email + WordPress.com followers); email is the subset that receives email; paid is the subset on a paid newsletter plan. Numbers are fetched from WordPress.com and cached locally for one hour, so transient network errors yield a stale-but-non-zero response when one is available. Requires an active Jetpack connection — sites without one return jetpack_newsletter_not_connected.'=>'Return aggregate subscriber counts for the site. Always returns { all: int, email: int, paid: int }: all is the total subscriber count (email + WordPress.com followers); email is the subset that receives email; paid is the subset on a paid newsletter plan. Numbers are fetched from WordPress.com and cached locally for one hour, so transient network errors yield a stale-but-non-zero response when one is available. Requires an active Jetpack connection — sites without one return jetpack_newsletter_not_connected.','Get Newsletter subscriber stats'=>'Get Newsletter subscriber stats','Names of the fields that actually changed during this call. Empty when the call was a no-op.'=>'Names of the fields that actually changed during this call. Empty when the call was a no-op.','Update one or more Jetpack Newsletter settings. Any subset of the five fields may be supplied; omitted fields are left untouched. Idempotent — fields whose desired value already matches the current value are not rewritten. Returns { settings: <full current state after the update>, changed: <array of field names that actually transitioned> }. An empty input or input matching the current state returns changed = [].'=>'Update one or more Jetpack Newsletter settings. Any subset of the five fields may be supplied; omitted fields are left untouched. Idempotent — fields whose desired value already matches the current value are not rewritten. Returns { settings: <full current state after the update>, changed: <array of field names that actually transitioned> }. An empty input or input matching the current state returns changed = [].','Update Newsletter settings'=>'Update Newsletter settings','Return the current Jetpack Newsletter settings as a flat object. Always returns the same five fields: subscribe_post_end_enabled (bool), subscribe_comments_enabled (bool), notify_admin_on_subscribe (bool), reply_to ("comment"|"author"|"no-reply"), and from_name (string). Read-only and idempotent. To change any value, call jetpack-newsletter/update-settings.'=>'Return the current Jetpack Newsletter settings as a flat object. Always returns the same five fields: subscribe_post_end_enabled (bool), subscribe_comments_enabled (bool), notify_admin_on_subscribe (bool), reply_to ("comment"|"author"|"no-reply"), and from_name (string). Read-only and idempotent. To change any value, call jetpack-newsletter/update-settings.','Get Newsletter settings'=>'Get Newsletter settings','Sender name shown on newsletter emails. Empty string falls back to the site name.'=>'Sender name shown on newsletter emails. Empty string falls back to the site name.','Reply-to address for newsletter emails. "comment" routes to the post comment author, "author" to the post author, "no-reply" disables replies. Default "comment".'=>'Reply-to address for newsletter emails. "comment" routes to the post comment author, "author" to the post author, "no-reply" disables replies. Default "comment".','Email the site admin whenever a new subscriber signs up. Default true.'=>'Email the site admin whenever a new subscriber signs up. Default true.','Show a "notify me of new comments" checkbox in the comment form. Default true.'=>'Show a "notify me of new comments" checkbox in 