file was provided.'=>'No plugin zip file was provided.','Uploaded attachment is not a .zip file.'=>'Uploaded attachment is not a .zip file.','Uploaded attachment is not a zip package.'=>'Uploaded attachment is not a zip package.','The referenced upload does not belong to the current user.'=>'The referenced upload does not belong to the current user.','The referenced upload is not a valid attachment.'=>'The referenced upload is not a valid attachment.','Unknown top-content type.'=>'Unknown top-content type.','Unknown role `%1$s` in `%2$s`. Known roles: %3$s.'=>'Unknown role `%1$s` in `%2$s`. Known roles: %3$s.','Role slugs in `%1$s` must be non-empty strings. Known roles: %2$s.'=>'Role slugs in `%1$s` must be non-empty strings. Known roles: %2$s.','Field `%s` must be an array of role slugs.'=>'Field `%s` must be an array of role slugs.','Provide at least one of: %s.'=>'Provide at least one of: %s.','Follower data could not be fetched from WordPress.com. Confirm the site is connected and try again.'=>'Follower data could not be fetched from WordPress.com. Confirm the site is connected and try again.','A positive post_id is required.'=>'A positive post_id is required.','A `type` is required. Valid values: %s.'=>'A `type` is required. Valid values: %s.','Stats data could not be fetched from WordPress.com. Confirm the site is connected and try again.'=>'Stats data could not be fetched from WordPress.com. Confirm the site is connected and try again.','Whether to honor the browser Do Not Track header.'=>'Whether to honor the browser Do Not Track header.','Role slugs whose visits are counted. May be empty (count visits from all users).'=>'Role slugs whose visits are counted. May be empty (count visits from all users).','Whether to show the Stats item in the admin bar for users who can view Stats.'=>'Whether to show the Stats item in the toolbar for users who can view Stats.','Update one or more Jetpack Stats settings. All fields are optional; only fields present in the call are written, and unrelated keys are preserved. Idempotent — setting a value to its current state returns changed=false. Shape: { changed, settings: { admin_bar, roles, count_roles, do_not_track } }. Role slugs added to `roles` or `count_roles` must be registered roles on the site; unknown slugs return jetpack_stats_invalid_role. A slug that is already saved is kept even when its role no longer exists. Narrowing `roles` can revoke Stats access for whole groups of users — confirm with the user before removing roles.'=>'Update one or more Jetpack Stats settings. All fields are optional; only fields present in the call are written, and unrelated keys are preserved. Idempotent — setting a value to its current state returns changed=false. Shape: { changed, settings: { admin_bar, roles, count_roles, do_not_track } }. Role slugs added to `roles` or `count_roles` must be registered roles on the site; unknown slugs return jetpack_stats_invalid_role. A slug that is already saved is kept even when its role no longer exists. Narrowing `roles` can revoke Stats access for whole groups of users — confirm with the user before removing roles.','Update Stats settings'=>'Update Stats settings','Read the current Jetpack Stats settings: who sees the Stats admin bar + menu, whose visits are counted, and DNT behavior. Shape: { admin_bar, roles, count_roles, do_not_track }. `roles` is an array of role slugs that can view Stats; `count_roles` is an array of role slugs whose visits are counted. Call jetpack-stats/update-settings to change any of these.'=>'Read the current Jetpack Stats settings: who sees the Stats admin bar + menu, whose visits are counted, and DNT behavior. Shape: { admin_bar, roles, count_roles, do_not_track }. `roles` is an array of role slugs that can view Stats; `count_roles` is an array of role slugs whose visits are counted. Call jetpack-stats/update-settings to change any of these.','Get Stats settings'=>'Get Stats settings','Return a breakdown of follower counts across email, WordPress.com, comment, and publicize (per-service) — answers "how is my audience growing?" in one call. Shape: { total, email, wpcom, comment, publicize: { <service>: count }, partial: bool, errors?: [string] }. Composes three WPCOM endpoints — if any sub-call fails, `partial` is true and `errors` lists the failed sub-calls; when `partial` is true, source counts owned by the failed sub-call(s) are placeholder zeros rather than confirmed zero counts (cross-reference `errors` before treating a `0` as authoritative). Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com.'=>'Return a breakdown of follower counts across email, WordPress.com, comment, and publicize (per-service) — answers "how is my audience growing?" in one call. Shape: { total, email, wpcom, comment, publicize: { <service>: count }, partial: bool, errors?: [string] }. Composes three WPCOM endpoints — if any sub-call fails, `partial` is true and `errors` lists the failed sub-calls; when `partial` is true, source counts owned by the failed sub-call(s) are placeholder zeros rather than confirmed zero counts (cross-reference `errors` before treating a `0` as authoritative). Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com.','Get follower counts'=>'Get follower counts','Which metrics to include in each row. Defaults to views+visitors.'=>'Which metrics to include in each row. Defaults to views+visitors.','How many data points to return (1-90).'=>'How many data points to return (1-90).','Granularity of each data point.'=>'Granularity of each data point.','Return a site-level views/visitors/likes/comments timeseries — answers "is traffic trending up?". Shape: { unit, quantity, date, fields, series: [ { date, views, visitors, likes, comments } ] }. Every series row always includes every field listed in the request (no per-row omission). Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com.'=>'Return a site-level views/visitors/likes/comments timeseries — answers "is traffic trending up?". Shape: { unit, quantity, date, fields, series: [ { date, views, visitors, likes, comments } ] }. Every series row always includes every field listed in the request (no per-row omission). Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com.','Get site visits timeseries'=>'Get site visits timeseries','How many prior periods to include (1-90).'=>'How many prior periods to include (1-90).','The post ID to fetch views for. Must be positive.'=>'The post ID to fetch views for. Must be positive.','Return views history for a single post: total views, timeseries of per-period views, and the period metadata. Shape: { post_id, total_views, period, num, date, series: [ { date, views } ] }. Accepts post_id as integer or numeric string (the literal "0" is rejected only because WordPress has no post 0 — any positive numeric value is legal). Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com. Related: call jetpack-stats/get-top-content with type=posts first to discover which posts to drill into.'=>'Return views history for a single post: total views, timeseries of per-period views, and the period metadata. Shape: { post_id, total_views, period, num, date, series: [ { date, views } ] }. Accepts post_id as integer or numeric string (the literal "0" is rejected only because WordPress has no post 0 — any positive numeric value is legal). Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com. Related: call jetpack-stats/get-top-content with type=posts first to discover which posts to drill into.','Get views for a post'=>'Get views for a post','Results cap (1-100).'=>'Results cap (1-100).','How many prior periods to roll up (1-90).'=>'How many prior periods to roll up (1-90).','End date (YYYY-MM-DD). Defaults to today.'=>'End date (YYYY-MM-DD). Defaults to today.','Aggregation period.'=>'Aggregation period.','Which top-N surface to fetch.'=>'Which top-N surface to fetch.','Return the top items for a chosen content type — posts, referrers, search terms, outbound clicks, tags/categories, authors, countries, downloads, or video plays — in one filtered call. Replaces nine atomic WPCOM endpoints with a single ability. Uniform shape: { type, period, date, num, max, items: [ { rank, label, value, href? } ] } — agents MUST NOT see a different shape per type. `label` is human-readable (post title, referrer host, search term, country name, etc.). `value` is the view/hit count for that item. `href` is present only when the item has a canonical URL. Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com.'=>'Return the top items for a chosen content type — posts, referrers, search terms, outbound clicks, tags/categories, authors, countries, downloads, or video plays — in one filtered call. Replaces nine atomic WPCOM endpoints with a single ability. Uniform shape: { type, period, date, num, max, items: [ { rank, label, value, href? } ] } — agents MUST NOT see a different shape per type. `label` is human-readable (post title, referrer host, search term, country name, etc.). `value` is the view/hit count for that item. `href` is present only when the item has a canonical URL. Precondition: site must be connected to WordPress.com.','Get top stats content'=>'Get top stats content','Return a single zero-argument snapshot answering "how is my site doing right now?" — today\'s views/visitors, this week/month totals, the current posting streak, today\'s top post, and top referrer. Shape: { date, views_today, visitors_today, views_week, views_month, streak: { current_length, longest_length, longest_start, longest_end }, top_post: { id, title, views }, top_referrer: { name, views }, partial: bool, errors?: [string] }. Composes the WPCOM stats/summary, stats/highlights, and stats/streak endpoints — if any sub-call fails, `partial` is true and `errors` lists the failed sub-calls; when `partial` is true, count fields owned by the failed sub-call(s) are placeholder zeros rather than confirmed counts (cross-reference `errors` before treating a `0` as authoritative). If every sub-call fails, returns `jetpack_stats_data_unavailable`. Precondition: the site must be connected to WordPress.com. Results cached for ~5 minutes by WPCOM_Stats — safe to poll.'=>'Return a single zero-argument snapshot answering "how is my site doing right now?" — today\'s views/visitors, this week/month totals, the current posting streak, today\'s top post, and top referrer. Shape: { date, views_today, visitors_today, views_week, views_month, streak: { current_length, longest_length, longest_start, longest_end }, top_post: { id, title, views }, top_referrer: { name, views }, partial: bool, errors?: [string] }. Composes the WPCOM stats/summary, stats/highlights, and stats/streak endpoints — if any sub-call fails, `partial` is true and `errors` lists the failed sub-calls; when `partial` is true, count fields owned by the failed sub-call(s) are placeholder zeros rather than confirmed counts (cross-reference `errors` before treating a `0` as authoritative). If every sub-call fails, returns `jetpack_stats_data_unavailable`. Precondition: the site must be connected to WordPress.com. Results cached for ~5 minutes by WPCOM_Stats — safe to poll.','Get site stats overview'=>'Get site stats overview','Abilities for reading Jetpack Stats traffic insights and managing site-level Stats settings.'=>'Abilities for reading Jetpack Stats traffic insights and managing site-level Stats settings.','list'=>'list','A compact Jetpack Search toolbar with inline filter and sort controls, plus a dense result list.'=>'A compact Jetpack Search toolbar with inline filter and sort controls, plus a dense result list.','Compact Search'=>'Compact Search','jetpack search'=>'jetpack search','results'=>'results','blog'=>'blog','search'=>'search','A full-page search layout with sidebar filters and a result list powered by Jetpack Search.'=>'A full-page search layout with sidebar filters and a result list powered by Jetpack Search.','Blog Search Page'=>'Blog Search Page','Remove %s'=>'Remove %s','Found %d